        <p class="profile-detail-region">Battle · Central &amp; East Asia</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battles of Khalkhin Gol</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">11 May to 15 September 1939; the cease-fire agreed on 15 September took effect at 1:10 pm on 16 September. The main Soviet offensive began on 20 August</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">Along the river Khalkhin Gol near Nomonhan, on the disputed border between the Mongolian People's Republic and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchukuo">Manchukuo</a>, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgy-zhukov">Georgy Zhukov</a>, with about 50,000 Soviet and Mongolian soldiers in the attack on the east bank on 20 August; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchukuo">Manchukuo</a>, with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwantung-army">Kwantung Army</a>'s 23rd Infantry Division under Lieutenant General Michitarō Komatsubara at the point of contact</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">Soviet victory: the Japanese forces on the Mongolian side of the border were destroyed by 31 August, and a cease-fire followed on 15 September.</span></div>
        </div>
